---
import Ornament from "./Ornament.astro";
---

<article class="cv-sheet" aria-labelledby="cv-title">
  <div class="cv-frame-ornament cv-frame-tl"><Ornament kind="frame-corner" /></div>
  <div class="cv-frame-ornament cv-frame-tr"><Ornament kind="frame-corner" /></div>
  <div class="cv-frame-ornament cv-frame-bl"><Ornament kind="frame-corner" /></div>
  <div class="cv-frame-ornament cv-frame-br"><Ornament kind="frame-corner" /></div>
  <header class="cv-heading">
    <Ornament kind="divider" />
    <h1 id="cv-title">Tyler Kleint</h1>
    <p class="cv-subtitle">Linux systems administrator &amp; software developer.</p>
    <address class="cv-contact">
      Bronx, New York · <a href="mailto:tyleralk@gmail.com">tyleralk@gmail.com</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/OffensiveGeneric" rel="me">GitHub</a> ·
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tyler-laboe-kleint/" rel="me">LinkedIn</a>
    </address>
  </header>

  <div class="cv-body">
    <section class="cv-section">
      <h2>Profile</h2>
      <div><p>Linux systems administrator and Computer Science graduate with experience supporting university research and instructional computing for up to 60 concurrent users across an approximately 15-computer, Kubernetes-connected lab. Experienced with Ubuntu, JupyterHub, Nginx, Bash/SSH automation, VMware, and hybrid Azure/AWS infrastructure.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="cv-section">
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <div class="cv-scroll-ornament" aria-hidden="true"><Ornament kind="vertical-vine" /><Ornament kind="vine" /></div>
      <div class="cv-entries">
        <article><div class="cv-entry-meta">Jan. 2020—<br />Dec. 2024</div><div><h3>Junior Systems Administrator</h3><p class="cv-employer">The City College of New York, Computer Science Department · New York, NY</p><ul><li>Supported an approximately 15-computer, Kubernetes-connected lab environment serving up to 60 concurrent research and instructional users.</li><li>Deployed Linux servers, multi-user JupyterHub instances, Nginx reverse proxies, TLS certificates, and Let’s Encrypt access.</li><li>Developed Bash automation for remote SSH connections and administered DNS, DHCP, LDAP, VMware, and monitoring tooling.</li><li>Supported hybrid Azure, AWS, and on-premises infrastructure.</li></ul></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="cv-section">
      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <div class="cv-scroll-ornament" aria-hidden="true"><Ornament kind="vertical-vine" /><Ornament kind="vine" /></div>
      <div class="cv-entries">
        <article><div class="cv-entry-meta">2026</div><div><h3><a href="https://github.com/OffensiveGeneric/tyler-site">Tyler Kleint Personal Site</a></h3><p class="cv-employer">Astro engineering and visual-design project</p><ul><li>Built a server-rendered Astro and TypeScript site with semantic HTML, scoped and container-aware CSS, and native view transitions.</li><li>Created an accessible responsive-image workflow that generates AVIF and WebP derivatives for photography and writing.</li><li>Deployed the Node application behind Caddy on an Ubuntu DigitalOcean host with automated health checks and releases.</li></ul></div></article>
        <article><div class="cv-entry-meta">2026</div><div><h3><a href="https://github.com/OffensiveGeneric/exo">Distributed AI Infrastructure</a></h3><p class="cv-employer">CCNY GlassLab</p><ul><li>Configured two Apple Silicon Mac Studio nodes for distributed MLX inference over Thunderbolt using JACCL.</li><li>Built distributed test harnesses for rank assignment, ring communication, and collective completion.</li><li>Established static networking and SSH forwarding between macOS model servers and a Linux orchestration client.</li></ul></div></article>
        <article><div class="cv-entry-meta">2025—26</div><div><h3><a href="https://github.com/OffensiveGeneric/ADNS">ADNS — Anomaly Detection Network System</a></h3><p class="cv-employer">Senior Project</p><ul><li>Designed Python ingestion services and a Flask/Gunicorn backend for network-flow data and REST endpoints.</li><li>Implemented Isolation Forest anomaly scoring, database/API architecture, and a React/Vite monitoring dashboard.</li><li>Deployed the system to DigitalOcean Ubuntu using Nginx, systemd, and SSH.</li></ul></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="cv-section">
      <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
      <div><p class="cv-list">Linux · Ubuntu · Kubernetes · JupyterHub · Nginx · VMware<br />TCP/IP · DNS · DHCP · LDAP · SSH · TLS · Let’s Encrypt<br />Azure · AWS · DigitalOcean · Bash · Python · MLX · JACCL<br />Flask · Gunicorn · REST APIs · PostgreSQL · MySQL · React/Vite · Git · FastAPI · LM Studio</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="cv-section">
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <div><h3 class="cv-education">B.S., Computer Science</h3><p>The City College of New York · December 2025</p></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <footer class="cv-colophon">Built with Astro, semantic HTML, modern CSS, SQLite, and an AVIF/WebP image pipeline.</footer>
</article>
